*Bold* refers to configurations supported by the DICOM specification. _TIFF?_ refers to codecs that have been granted a TIFF compression tag, but are not widely supported by TIFF readers, whereas _TIFF_ refers to codecs that are widely supported by TIFF readers. Note that TIFF is a container format and can contain codecs that have not been granted a TIFF compression tag. If the _Unsuitable Reason_ column is not empty, the codec has been deemed unsuitable for inclusion in this study on the basis of the reason provided.